cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Nucleation Pilot & Related Projects: A Frozen White-Box Detector for Persistent Manipulation, Its Cross-Family Transfer, and Preregistered Methods"
abstract: >-
  A frozen, SHA-256-hashed linear detector reads whether an early manipulation is still
  "live" in a language model's residual stream. Validated once on an owned toy (held-out
  AUC 0.807), it transfers causally and source-decoupled to six independently-built
  open-weight families, carries to a naturalistic in-context frame (Config-E), and returns
  a firm null on an honest owned-model refusal-erosion attempt (Config-D). Benign
  open-weight lane throughout; no exploit content.
type: software
